{"school":{"dbn":"32K383","name":"J.H.S. 383 Philippa Schuyler","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"32","district_label":"District 32","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"5 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":648,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"1300 GREENE AVENUE, BROOKLYN, NY 11237","phone":"718-642-4890","website":null,"directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63740","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Students at our school are assigned instructional programs that meet their individual gifts and talents. Philippa Schuyler offers a variety of acceleration and enrichment opportunities that include advanced language arts and math classes, Regents classes in Algebra, Living Environmnent, Earth Science, French and Spanish.  Major performing arts courses are offered in a variety of dance styles including jazz, modern, ballet, world and urban dance.  Additional major performing arts courses include: theater, theater tech and design, film, steel pan, modern band and chorus.  Other electives include: technology, STEAM, hydroponic gardening, sustainability, and debate.  We offer preparation courses for Specialized High School testing.  Our school offeres a bilingual/dual language program in Spanish.  Our school has a stat of the art hydroponics science lab and Maker Space.  Our instructional program focuses on project-based instruction and assessment to promote rigorous critical-thinking and citizenship skills.","start_time":"08:19am","end_time":"02:39pm","languages":null,"subway":"L to DeKalb Av; M to Knickerbocker Av","bus":"B13, B26, B38, B52, B54, B60, Q55, Q58","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Bushwick","latitude":40.6978,"longitude":-73.9193,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.921],"n":[386.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","20